[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563033689","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2563033689","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2563033689,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YxMpZ","user":{"login":"drcucaracha","id":49615968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjE1OTY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49615968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/drcucaracha","html_url":"https://github.com/drcucaracha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drcucaracha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drcucaracha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drcucaracha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drcucaracha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drcucaracha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drcucaracha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drcucaracha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drcucaracha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/drcucaracha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T19:06:28Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T19:06:28Z","body":"Hi, could you add something like a label to know how much video memory and RAM is consumed by the application/game?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563033689/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563035730","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2563035730","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2563035730,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YxNJS","user":{"login":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T19:09:19Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T19:12:53Z","body":"I'm not sure it makes sense to color-code the entire bottom section of text based on the currently used rendering method. That same range of color hues (blue, green at least, arguably the vaguely red color for Mobile) is already used to indicate performance elsewhere in the UI. I think colorcoding just the renderer name or the line it is on might make more sense.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563035730/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563044732","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2563044732","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2563044732,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YxPV8","user":{"login":"RedMser","id":5117197,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTcxOTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5117197?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser","html_url":"https://github.com/RedMser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RedMser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T19:24:59Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T19:25:41Z","body":"While this feature will be largely useful to many people, I don't really agree with the way it is implemented here. It feels very inflexible and too tightly coupled to SceneTree.\r\n\r\nWouldn't it be enough to expose the `DebugMenu` class (or however it'll be named) as a node you can add to your game?\r\nThis way you have full control over when it is visible, you can export properties on it which can be modified (e.g. styling, turning display mode into multiple booleans, position, etc.) and you could even insert it into multiple different viewports at once for split-screen or multi-window games (currently just the main window can have the overlay visible it seems).\r\nFor simple cases, the user may just add it as an Autoload so it hooks to the main window like in the current implementation.\r\n\r\nThis means the SceneTree API, the input map changes and the ProjectSettings changes could all be reverted. The class is exposed to ClassDB. Some logic that currently assumes that the node never moves would also need updating (e.g. detecting reparenting for `viewport_node size_changed` signal).\r\n\r\nAnd in turn it would then require the user to add the node to an appropriate location by hand, and to use scripting to show/hide the overlay instead of a magic built-in action.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563044732/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563084409","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2563084409","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2563084409,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YxZB5","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T20:35:19Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T20:40:25Z","body":"> Wouldn't it be enough to expose the DebugMenu class (or however it'll be named) as a node you can add to your game?\r\n\r\nI've thought about it, but then it's no longer automatically available in every project out of the box. This is an issue when testing MRPs or working on prototypes, as having to configure it manually in every of these projects would get tedious quickly. I understand the concerns about tight coupling, but having good integration/UX for this is paramount if you want people to be able to use it early on in their projects. Without having this in place, having this in core is only slightly easier than using the existing add-on.\r\n\r\nThere might be an argument for splitscreen or multi-window but from what I've seen, all these debug overlays are common across all viewports in other engines/games. The information they report doesn't change from viewport to viewport after all, with the exception of resolution (but in splitscreen games, it's often the same across all viewports anyway - just a divisor of the fullscreen size). For non-game applications (the main user of multiple window support), they aren't as likely to use a debug overlay like this in the first place.\r\n\r\nNote that the node is dynamically added by SceneTree, so there is no performance or memory cost when the debug menu isn't visible (it's freed once you hide it and recreated when needed).\r\n\r\n> I'm not sure it makes sense to color-code the entire bottom section of text based on the currently used rendering method. That same range of color hues (blue, green at least, arguably the vaguely red color for Mobile) is already used to indicate performance elsewhere in the UI. I think colorcoding just the renderer name or the line it is on might make more sense.\r\n\r\nThat can be done, it'll just need splitting the rendering method line to its own node.\r\n\r\n> Hi, could you add something like a label to know how much video memory and RAM is consumed by the application/game?\r\n\r\nThis needs https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/4871 to be implemented first, along with another API to query the amount of VRAM used by the game. Only RenderingDevice-based rendering methods will be able to implement this, as OpenGL has no standard API for this.\r\n\r\nRegarding RAM utilization, Godot has some debug counters available for this, but in my experience, it doesn't accurately reflect the RAM used by the whole Godot process (I'm not sure why). If you compare what you see in the Windows task manager for instance, what Godot reports will often be a fair bit lower than what's reported in the task manager. I would need to make sure what it's reporting is 100% accurate before we expose this information in the debug menu, as displaying misleading information is worse than not displaying any information.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563084409/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563087352","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2563087352","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2563087352,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YxZv4","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T20:41:15Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T20:41:15Z","body":"The only thing I know for sure - this one will be great addition for Game Editor/Workspace. Other questions (should it be separate node accessable by users (including in exported release builds), which data it should provide and so on) are still opened.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563087352/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563096072","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2563096072","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2563096072,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yxb4I","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T20:58:27Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T20:58:27Z","body":"> Prevent DebugMenu nodes from being selectable in the game editor (as they can get in the way). @YeldhamDev Is there some kind of node metadata available for this?\r\n\r\nNot currently, no. If such system would be implemented, it would also need to prevent it appearing in the remote tree as well.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563096072/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563098241","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2563098241","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2563098241,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6YxcaB","user":{"login":"timoschwarzer","id":8849554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDk1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8849554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer","html_url":"https://github.com/timoschwarzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T21:02:35Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T21:02:35Z","body":"It would be nice if this would be somehow expandable by user code.\r\n (`DebugMenuPlugin`?). I'm thinking of stuff like network latency for other games or general debug information that is specific to the game (scene management, 3rd party integrations like FMOD etc.pp.).\r\nIn split screen games (i.e. subviewports) the time it took to render that specific viewport would be interesting.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563098241/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563165546","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2563165546","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2563165546,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yxs1q","user":{"login":"ckaiser","id":138269,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODI2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138269?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ckaiser","html_url":"https://github.com/ckaiser","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ckaiser/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ckaiser/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ckaiser/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ckaiser/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ckaiser/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ckaiser/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ckaiser/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ckaiser/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ckaiser/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-26T23:22:05Z","updated_at":"2024-12-26T23:22:05Z","body":"Tested on Windows, works as intended. I've been using your extension on most of my projects so having this built in would be great! 🥳 \r\n\r\nSomething I noticed but that is purely personal preference is that I like the old colors a bit better, it looks more contrasty and the green seems to over-highlight text that really isn't that important and doesn't change much.\r\n\r\n![extension_v_inbuilt](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/955f5c39-0fd6-4d27-b7d7-370e68e12263)\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563165546/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563448461","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2563448461","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2563448461,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Yyx6N","user":{"login":"Alexofp","id":14040378,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDQwMzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14040378?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp","html_url":"https://github.com/Alexofp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexofp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T08:21:28Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T08:21:28Z","body":"![pic](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8a21043d-9f6a-49ef-8c2f-70ee368e68b4)\r\n\r\nGreat plugin, would be incredibly useful to have in the engine, I would love if there was a way to show how many drawcalls, gpu memory and triangles are being pushed to the renderer. Very important info when you're trying to optimize your game\r\nI modified the gdscript plugin to show that info and it's been perfect for me. Would be nice to have these options (maybe optionally) somewhere here if it's gonna be added..","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563448461/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563800682","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2563800682","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2563800682,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y0H5q","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-27T15:26:26Z","updated_at":"2024-12-27T15:27:30Z","body":"> I would love if there was a way to show how many drawcalls, gpu memory and triangles are being pushed to the renderer. Very important info when you're trying to optimize your game\r\n\r\nThis information is only reported for 3D currently (it doesn't take anything 2D into account), so it would be irrelevant for 2D projects. If it was to be added to the debug menu, it'd have to be a project setting you manually enable, or we could hide it if the reported draw call/primitive count is 0.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2563800682/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2570215157","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100829#issuecomment-2570215157","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100829","id":2570215157,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZMl71","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repo